# Ansible Quality Rules

- Prefer fully qualified `ansible.builtin.*` modules.
- Avoid `shell`/`command` when an appropriate module exists.
- When `command`/`shell` is genuinely necessary, make changed-state and failure-state explicit and testable.
- User-facing variables use `bootstrap_*`.
- Keep role-internal variables private to the role.
- Second identical apply must result in `changed=0`.
- Do not rewrite equivalent files merely to update timestamps.
- Support useful non-mutating check mode where technically honest.
- Validate inputs before mutation.
- Use handlers only when a real state change requires them.
- Avoid unconditional service restarts.
- Critical configuration should follow candidate -> validate -> activate -> reload/verify patterns where practical.
- Prefer small responsibility-oriented roles over one giant role or excessive micro-roles.
- Do not add support for non-MVP distributions.
